# libCarPlayCore: AirPlayReceiverSessionScreen_ProcessFrames reads each screen frame's header and body with NetSocket's special timeout -65536, which TCC's NetSocket_Wait turns into 200 ms: one 200 ms gap inside a frame (a Wi-Fi retransmit) stops the screen stream ("screen stream timeout - body", black CarPlay screen). Wired USB never gaps that long. Here the reads wait up to 5 s instead (movs r7,#5 / movt r7,#0). EV6 KR 260902
# HMG-API applies only the first recipe in a library's list that fits its build: this one goes before carplay-core-wifi, whose "native" line matches the same KR v039 library (it accepts Wi-Fi sessions as it is), so the KR library gets this patch and loses nothing (11th collection: listed second, it never ran)
